(1437412, 185945, 6349, '<td valign="top">I like this photo a lot.  The use of the "frame" in this is interesting.  I can''t decide how I feel about it.  On one hand it seems to be framing the hand and belt buckle, which would make an interesting image all on their own, but I feel that in this case the face/hat is where the character is.  On the other hand, I feel the shot would be much less interesting if it wasn''t shot through the foreground gate.  It gives it a more natural and candid feeling.  Screw it.  What the hell I''m I talking about.  I''m giving it a 10 and adding it to my favorites.  The more I look at it the more I love it.</td>', 'I like this photo a lot.  The use of the "frame" in this is interesting.  I can''t decide how I feel about it.  On one hand it seems to be framing the hand and belt buckle, which would make an interesting image all on their own, but I feel that in this case the face/hat is where the character is.  On the other hand, I feel the shot would be much less interesting if it wasn''t shot through the foreground gate.  It gives it a more natural and candid feeling.  Screw it.  What the hell I''m I talking about.  I''m giving it a 10 and adding it to my favorites.  The more I look at it the more I love it.', '2005-06-06 18:44:28.000000', NULL, 1),
