(1438282, 185807, 38793, '<td valign="top">This is the most amazing photograph I have ever seen.  I don''t know much about photography, but this photo blows my mind.  Way to go, I hope you win!  I didn''t even notice the window frame within the eye until my 15th time viewing the photo. I orginally thought that the eyball was framing the iris, or the fur was fraiming the lens and the eye was the windo in which the cast used to see out of.  Once again this photo is AMAZING!</td>', 'This is the most amazing photograph I have ever seen.  I don''t know much about photography, but this photo blows my mind.  Way to go, I hope you win!  I didn''t even notice the window frame within the eye until my 15th time viewing the photo. I orginally thought that the eyball was framing the iris, or the fur was fraiming the lens and the eye was the windo in which the cast used to see out of.  Once again this photo is AMAZING!', '2005-06-07 03:48:11.000000', NULL, 1),
