(1446855, 185789, 25140, '<td valign="top">Wow, I like the color palette but they are too intense, its a bit unnatural.  The detail on the branch is nice and it makes a lovely natural frame.</td>', 'Wow, I like the color palette but they are too intense, its a bit unnatural.  The detail on the branch is nice and it makes a lovely natural frame.', '2005-06-10 23:13:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(1446857, 184201, 25140, '<td valign="top">I really like the simple beauty in this photo.  I like the soft textures and colors, they are such nice complements.</td>', 'I really like the simple beauty in this photo.  I like the soft textures and colors, they are such nice complements.', '2005-06-10 23:17:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(1446862, 185828, 25140, '<td valign="top">Your photo is balanced so nicely.  You''ve placed the rocks high enough in the frame so they seem light, like they are floating.  They work with the clouds above to create a nice natural frame for the islands and the birds.  Simple beauty, great work.</td>', 'Your photo is balanced so nicely.  You''ve placed the rocks high enough in the frame so they seem light, like they are floating.  They work with the clouds above to create a nice natural frame for the islands and the birds.  Simple beauty, great work.', '2005-06-10 23:22:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(1446864, 185857, 25140, '<td valign="top">What a lovely subject and frame.  The focus is a little soft.  If you use a slower shutter speed with a tripod you could have the trees and rocks in sharp focus, while the falls would turn into a misty motion blur.</td>', 'What a lovely subject and frame.  The focus is a little soft.  If you use a slower shutter speed with a tripod you could have the trees and rocks in sharp focus, while the falls would turn into a misty motion blur.', '2005-06-10 23:28:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1446866, 186045, 4281, '<td valign="top">Nice capture - good framing and it  even looks quite dreamy. I would like the bottom part of the asphalt to be a bit darker though, a slight burning would do nicely.<br/>Perhaps a slightly smaller aperture would have been better, it seems the asphalt above the truck is too much out of focus, though it could just be that it is covered with water?</td>', 'Nice capture - good framing and it  even looks quite dreamy. I would like the bottom part of the asphalt to be a bit darker though, a slight burning would do nicely.Perhaps a slightly smaller aperture would have been better, it seems the asphalt above the truck is too much out of focus, though it could just be that it is covered with water?', '2005-06-10 23:30:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(1446872, 185274, 25140, '<td valign="top">This is such an interesting photo, it really holds your attention.  I love the texture of the rock, the colors, and the shadows.  You''ve done a nice job of capturing an image with a subtle natural frame that works.</td>', 'This is such an interesting photo, it really holds your attention.  I love the texture of the rock, the colors, and the shadows.  You''ve done a nice job of capturing an image with a subtle natural frame that works.', '2005-06-10 23:35:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(1446875, 185728, 25140, '<td valign="top">I really like this, the shapes, forms and shadows make this photo appealing.</td>', 'I really like this, the shapes, forms and shadows make this photo appealing.', '2005-06-10 23:37:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1446878, 185556, 25140, '<td valign="top">This is an amazing shot.  Great work.  It has such nice DOF, colors, perspective, and of course, a great frame.  One of my favorites in this challenge.</td>', 'This is an amazing shot.  Great work.  It has such nice DOF, colors, perspective, and of course, a great frame.  One of my favorites in this challenge.', '2005-06-10 23:40:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(1446883, 185777, 4281, '<td valign="top">Here we have a good example of the value of fill-flash. The woman and the surrounding ''frame''  are simply too dark and you should have used the on-camera flash, or better yet an external flash, to lighten those parts  up a bit. <br/>It is often said that the built in flashes in cameras were put there for one reason, to be used as fill-flash  to lighten up the foreground during the day and not for using when there is little available light, such as in the evening.<br/> <br/>Try it! (If you haven''t done so yet). During sunny days you should try to enable the on-board flash when taking pictures of subjects close to the camera (especially people).</td>', 'Here we have a good example of the value of fill-flash. The woman and the surrounding ''frame''  are simply too dark and you should have used the on-camera flash, or better yet an external flash, to lighten those parts  up a bit. It is often said that the built in flashes in cameras were put there for one reason, to be used as fill-flash  to lighten up the foreground during the day and not for using when there is little available light, such as in the evening. Try it! (If you haven''t done so yet). During sunny days you should try to enable the on-board flash when taking pictures of subjects close to the camera (especially people).', '2005-06-10 23:44:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(1446885, 185407, 25140, '<td valign="top">Made me smile.  What a great shot, I like how the frog seems to be in a spotlight (and he''s lookin'' at me).  The glassy smooth water and the sharp lines of the grass make a really interesting frame with great texture.  The green color palette is nice.</td>', 'Made me smile.  What a great shot, I like how the frog seems to be in a spotlight (and he''s lookin'' at me).  The glassy smooth water and the sharp lines of the grass make a really interesting frame with great texture.  The green color palette is nice.', '2005-06-10 23:45:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(1446891, 185959, 25140, '<td valign="top">A great capture, the perspective and lighting are perfect.  Your natural frame is nice but some detail has been lost at the top, its seems a little dark.</td>', 'A great capture, the perspective and lighting are perfect.  Your natural frame is nice but some detail has been lost at the top, its seems a little dark.', '2005-06-10 23:50:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(1446898, 185994, 25140, '<td valign="top">I really like this shot, the steely color palette complements the red letters drawing my eye to the subjects.  The lines and shapes are interesting too.</td>', 'I really like this shot, the steely color palette complements the red letters drawing my eye to the subjects.  The lines and shapes are interesting too.', '2005-06-10 23:56:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(1446902, 185493, 25140, '<td valign="top">Your frame really invites the viewer to stroll down to the creek.  A nice photo with lovely soft colors.</td>', 'Your frame really invites the viewer to stroll down to the creek.  A nice photo with lovely soft colors.', '2005-06-10 23:58:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(1446906, 186073, 37730, '<td valign="top">beautiful</td>', 'beautiful', '2005-06-11 00:01:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(1447012, 185982, 19978, '<td valign="top">The tower at Antietam Battlefield! Great location for a shot but your pic looks woefully over processed, and as though the flash fired as you were looking through the window. The result looks very unnatural.</td>', 'The tower at Antietam Battlefield! Great location for a shot but your pic looks woefully over processed, and as though the flash fired as you were looking through the window. The result looks very unnatural.', '2005-06-11 01:47:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(1447015, 185789, 19978, '<td valign="top">Dramatic but I think you went too far. Preserving the natural color and hues of the original may have worked better.</td>', 'Dramatic but I think you went too far. Preserving the natural color and hues of the original may have worked better.', '2005-06-11 01:50:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(1447100, 185796, 26679, '<td valign="top">This is a great fram, the colours of the ecene look a little washed out. I think some adjustment  in saturation could lift this</td>', 'This is a great fram, the colours of the ecene look a little washed out. I think some adjustment  in saturation could lift this', '2005-06-11 03:29:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1447109, 185847, 26679, '<td valign="top">I like the way you have framed this, however I do ahave a few observations. I like my horozontals to either be perfectly horizontal, or more of an angle than yours shows, for me this is nomans land in the middle.<br/> <br/>Where you have selected the sky a tel tale white line has been left around the some of the leaves. This can be avoided by a number of techniques in photoshop.<br/>(If you have not got photoshop I appologise) " ctrl alt ~ " will  select the highlites - I assume this was a whitish sky then " Ctrl J " will set this up a a new layer. change blend mode to Multiply , this will make the highlights much darker, then adjust  opacity to gibe the result you wish.<br/> <br/>The other is to set up two layers. The fist a selective colour adjustment layer then the second a hue /saturation layer. This last one set master satutaion to zero. to same the image B/W.<br/> then on the selective colour play orounds with the blues to see if this changes the sky colour. <br/> <br/>T</td>', 'I like the way you have framed this, however I do ahave a few observations. I like my horozontals to either be perfectly horizontal, or more of an angle than yours shows, for me this is nomans land in the middle. Where you have selected the sky a tel tale white line has been left around the some of the leaves. This can be avoided by a number of techniques in photoshop.(If you have not got photoshop I appologise) " ctrl alt ~ " will  select the highlites - I assume this was a whitish sky then " Ctrl J " will set this up a a new layer. change blend mode to Multiply , this will make the highlights much darker, then adjust  opacity to gibe the result you wish. The other is to set up two layers. The fist a selective colour adjustment layer then the second a hue /saturation layer. This last one set master satutaion to zero. to same the image B/W. then on the selective colour play orounds with the blues to see if this changes the sky colour.  T', '2005-06-11 03:39:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1447151, 185084, 27399, '<td valign="top">Difficult shot to make: water line that bends, a mountainous horizon that isn''t level, and a tree (on the left) that doesn''t stand up straight . . . but you pulled it off well.  Good choice keeping the tree on the right partially in frame to give the appropriate orientation.  Nice title, too.</td>', 'Difficult shot to make: water line that bends, a mountainous horizon that isn''t level, and a tree (on the left) that doesn''t stand up straight . . . but you pulled it off well.  Good choice keeping the tree on the right partially in frame to give the appropriate orientation.  Nice title, too.', '2005-06-11 06:06:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1447152, 186040, 27399, '<td valign="top">Good work! The image feels like water is the "framed" area, with the goose/swan slightly out of frame but entering it.  I like it, nice soft image.</td>', 'Good work! The image feels like water is the "framed" area, with the goose/swan slightly out of frame but entering it.  I like it, nice soft image.', '2005-06-11 06:09:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(1447158, 185465, 27399, '<td valign="top">I love that technique, and the image is great.  But I''m missing a strong connection to the challenge.</td>', 'I love that technique, and the image is great.  But I''m missing a strong connection to the challenge.', '2005-06-11 06:12:50.000000', NULL, 1),
